---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { repoUrl } from '../config';
const baseUrl = (import.meta.env.BASE_URL || '/').replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Layout lang="en" title="About — OmniPrep" description="OmniPrep — unified multimodal MRI preprocessing and analysis pipeline." active="about">

    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="breadcrumb"><a href={`${baseUrl}/`}>Home</a><span class="sep">/</span>About</div>
        <h1>About OmniPrep</h1>
        <p class="lead">A unified, scalable, and robust pipeline for large-scale multimodal MRI preprocessing and analysis.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-layout container">
      <aside class="toc">
        <div class="toc-title">On this page</div>
        <ul>
          <li><a class="level-1" href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
          <li><a class="level-1" href="#principles">Design principles</a></li>
          <li><a class="level-1" href="#roadmap">Roadmap</a></li>
          <li><a class="level-1" href="#citation">Citation</a></li>
          <li><a class="level-1" href="#acknowledgements">Acknowledgements</a></li>
          <li><a class="level-1" href="#contributing">Contributing</a></li>
          <li><a class="level-1" href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
        </ul>
      </aside>

      <article class="doc-content prose">

        <section id="overview">
          <h2>Overview</h2>
          <img src={`${baseUrl}/assets/img/logo-full.svg`} alt="OmniPrep logo" style="max-width:340px;margin:0 auto 28px;display:block" />
          <p>
            OmniPrep is a unified neuroimaging pipeline that standardizes and preprocesses <strong>structural (sMRI)</strong>,
            <strong>functional (fMRI)</strong>, and <strong>diffusion (dMRI)</strong> MRI data within a single, coherent workflow.
            Built on <a href="https://www.nextflow.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nextflow</a>, it is containerized,
            resumable, and designed to scale from a single workstation to large HPC clusters and the cloud.
          </p>
          <p>
            Beyond preprocessing, OmniPrep generates analysis-ready derivatives: atlas- and ROI-level morphometric features,
            voxelwise and ROI functional metrics (ReHo, ALFF/fALFF, INT, time series, functional connectivity), and
            diffusion-derived tractography and structural connectomes — all with built-in quality control.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="principles">
          <h2>Design principles</h2>
          <div class="grid grid-2">
            <div class="card">
              <div class="card-icon blue">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 2v20M2 12h20"/></svg>
              </div>
              <h3>Unified</h3>
              <p>One command, one configuration surface, one output convention across sMRI, fMRI, and dMRI.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <div class="card-icon teal">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/></svg>
              </div>
              <h3>Scalable</h3>
              <p>Nextflow orchestrates work across local, cluster, and cloud executors without changing the interface.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <div class="card-icon orange">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 2l-2 2m-7.61 7.61a5.5 5.5 0 11-7.778 7.778 5.5 5.5 0 017.777-7.777zm0 0L15.5 7.5m0 0l3 3L22 7l-3-3m-3.5 3.5L19 4"/></svg>
              </div>
              <h3>Robust</h3>
              <p>Automatic age detection, adaptive templates and distortion-correction strategies, resumable runs, and selective error tolerance.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <div class="card-icon green">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 11-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg>
              </div>
              <h3>Reproducible</h3>
              <p>Containerized dependencies, BIDS input, standardized derivatives, and versioned QC artifacts.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="roadmap">
          <h2>Roadmap</h2>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>Milestone</th><th>Status</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Multimodal preprocessing (sMRI / fMRI / dMRI)</td><td><span class="badge badge-flag">active</span></td><td>Core workflow on Nextflow with Docker &amp; Singularity.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Atlas &amp; ROI derivatives</td><td><span class="badge badge-flag">active</span></td><td>Morphometry, ROI time series, FC &amp; structural connectomes.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Automated QC</td><td><span class="badge badge-flag">active</span></td><td>Run report, trace, timeline, motion scrubbing.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Interactive web UI</td><td><span class="badge badge-default">planned</span></td><td>Streamlit-based configuration front-end.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Expanded atlas catalog</td><td><span class="badge badge-default">planned</span></td><td>Additional cortical &amp; subcortical parcellations.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Group-level workflow</td><td><span class="badge badge-default">planned</span></td><td>Cohort-level aggregation and statistics.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="citation">
          <h2>Citation</h2>
          <p>If you use OmniPrep in your research, please cite the project (and the upstream tools it builds upon). A formal citation will be added upon publication.</p>
          <div class="code-block">
            <div class="cb-head"><span class="cb-label">bibtex</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
            <pre><code>@software&#123;omniprep,
  title   = &#123;OmniPrep: A Unified, Scalable, and Robust Pipeline for Large-Scale Multimodal MRI&#125;,
  author  = &#123;OmniPrep Contributors&#125;,
  year    = &#123;2026&#125;,
  url     = &#123;${repoUrl}&#125;
&#125;</code></pre>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="acknowledgements">
          <h2>Acknowledgements</h2>
          <p>
            OmniPrep builds on and is deeply indebted to the open neuroimaging community. Key dependencies and inspirations include:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://surfer.nmr.mgh.harvard.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FreeSurfer</a> — cortical reconstruction &amp; segmentation</li>
            <li><a href="https://fmriprep.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">fMRIPrep</a> / <a href="https://www.nipreps.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NiPreps</a> — preprocessing methodology</li>
            <li><a href="https://www.nextflow.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nextflow</a> — workflow orchestration</li>
            <li><a href="https://fsl.fmrib.ox.ac.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FSL</a> &amp; <a href="https://mrtrix.readthedocs.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MRtrix3</a> — distortion correction, tractography, connectomics</li>
            <li><a href="https://bids.neuroimaging.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BIDS</a> — the data standard OmniPrep consumes and respects</li>
            <li><a href="https://www.nitrc.org/projects/artifact_detect/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Power et al.</a> motion frame detection methodology</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="contributing">
          <h2>Contributing</h2>
          <p>
            OmniPrep is developed openly. Contributions — bug reports, feature requests, documentation improvements,
            and pull requests — are welcome. Please follow the project's contribution guidelines when submitting changes.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="contact">
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            For questions, feedback, or collaboration, open an issue on the project repository or reach out to the maintainers.
            Stay tuned for community channels as the project matures.
          </p>
        </section>

      </article>
    </section>
  
</Layout>
